  "source": "JoyPro curated on the maker's photo (2026-10-11), Sol-R 1 flightstick (white grip on the Sol-R 5 base) seen from behind (pilot's view) and slightly above, right-handed",
  "mappingSource": "Sol-R FlightStick user manual p.20-21 (https://ts.thrustmaster.com/download/accessories/Manuals/SOL-R/Sol-R_FlightStick_user-manual_21L.pdf), the identical grip page in the Sol-R 3 manual p.13 (https://ts.thrustmaster.com/download/accessories/Manuals/SOL-R/Sol-R_3_AVA_Add-On_Grip_user_manual.pdf) and the Sol-R 5 base manual p.18 (https://ts.thrustmaster.com/download/accessories/Manuals/SOL-R/Sol-R_5_BASE_User_Manual.pdf); the numbers printed on grip and base (30 40 35 39, 2 4 15 13, 5-8, 16-19, 9 10 11, 20-23) confirm them",
  "confidence": "high",
  "note": "Encoder 9 / 10: the manual and the printed double arrow do not say which turn direction is 9; the catalog cw = 9 / ccw = 10 is not confirmed (press 11 is). Catalog discrepancy: panel.button.1-4 and 12-15 (\"backlit button\") are the positions of the four 2-way switches (see the sol-r-base draft); 20-23 are the 4 positions of the right rotary selector. Possible catalog discrepancy on the scroll wheel: the manual figure stacks 37 / 36 / 38 with 36 in the middle (the wheel line points to 36), so 36 = push, 37 = up, 38 = down; the catalog has 36 = \"thumb wheel up\" and 37 = \"thumb wheel push\". The Sol-R 3 AVA manual p.15 draws the same wheel as 13 (top) / 14 (middle) / 15 (bottom); with the +23 offset between the two numberings (12 -> 35, 16 -> 39) that is 36 top / 37 middle, i.e. the catalog reading. The two Thrustmaster manuals contradict each other, so the two disputed wheel parts are set map=low until checked on a device. Handed: right-handed mode (0422). In left-handed mode (042A) the POV moves to the left hat (Sol-R 3 manual p.14), so trim hat / hat 2 swap. Trigger, front head lever (26/27) and pinky button (28) are on the front of the grip and hidden; the side lever on the left of the grip has no number.",
